              "content": "# MySQL Data Source Configuration Instructions\n\n## Demo Dashboard\nThis is a demo dashboard that shows how to configure the MySQL data source and includes a sample dashboard with a pre-configured query. You are already set up with the necessary access to view the sample panel shown below and create your own dashboards/panels using the same data source. However the configuration is shown in case you change these values or for any eventuality.\n\n## Required steps\n1. Request the instance configuration from the Azimut service's `/config` endpoint. This will provide you with the necessary credentials for the MySQL connection in the config.yml file.\n\n2. In Grafana, go to the left-hand menu and navigate to `/connections/datasources`\n\n3. Find and select the data source called \"Openedx MySQL\" and edit the following fields:\n   - Database name\n   - Username\n   - Password\n\n## Values to use in the configuration\n- **Database**: OPENEDX_MYSQL_DATABASE\n- **User**: OPENEDX_MYSQL_USERNAME\n- **Password**: OPENEDX_MYSQL_PASSWORD\n\n## Important notes\nExist a sample panel below will display data from your MySQL database. You can use this same data source configuration to create additional dashboards and panels.",
              "mode": "markdown"
            },
            "pluginVersion": "11.3.0",
            "title": "MySQL Datasource Configuration Instructions",
            "type": "text"
